-- title:
--   Corollary 2.6: Nondegeneracy of the central alternating form
-- statement:
--   All vector spaces and Lie algebras are finite dimensional and real, with their usual Hausdorff topology. An invariant set is invariant under the group generated by $e^{\operatorname{ad}y}$. A closed convex set is pointed when its recession edge is zero. Write $\mathcal O_x=\operatorname{Inn}(\mathfrak g)x$, $\operatorname{co}(x)=\overline{\operatorname{conv}}\mathcal O_x$, and $C_x=\operatorname{cone}(\mathcal O_x)$. Admissibility means existence of a pointed generating invariant closed convex subset.
--
--   Let $\mathfrak g=\mathfrak g(\mathfrak l,V,\mathfrak z,\beta)$ be an admissible algebra in its structural presentation. For every nonzero $v\in V$,
--
--   $$\exists w\in V:\quad\beta(v,w)=[v,w]\ne0.$$
--
--   This is nondegeneracy of the central-valued form; it does not assert nondegeneracy for every scalar functional. It underlies the kernel-image dualities.
-- source:
--   Elements in pointed invariant cones in Lie algebras and corresponding affine pairs, arXiv:2110.07297v1, PDF p. 5, Corollary 2.6: Nondegeneracy of the central alternating form

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Frontier30_P26

